/* Setup page subtitle */
"Vauta transcribes with Apple’s speech model, which runs on this Mac. It downloads once from Apple." = "Vauta 使用 Apple 语音识别模型在这台 Mac 上转录。模型只需从 Apple 下载一次。";

/* No comment provided by engineer. */
"Vauta transcribes your meetings on this Mac and turns them into minutes, decisions and tasks you can search and ask about." = "Vauta 在这台 Mac 上转录你的会议，整理成会⁠议⁠纪⁠要、决定和任务，供你搜索和提问。";

/* Settings → Models network server explanation */
"Vauta uses a model server on another computer on your local network, over HTTPS only. It never sends meetings to the internet." = "Vauta 使用本地网络中另一台电脑上的模型服务器，仅通过 HTTPS 连接。它绝不会将会议发送到互联网。";

/* About: the dependency statement; MLX (mlx-swift, MIT) is the one third-party package, and it runs the optional models Vauta downloads only on request. The button below it is “Credits and Licenses” */
"Vauta uses Apple frameworks, the SQLite library that comes with macOS, and MLX (mlx‑swift, MIT) with its swift‑numerics library (Apache 2.0). MLX runs the optional search and integrated models on this Mac; the models are downloaded only when you ask. Credits and Licenses lists everything." = "Vauta 使用 Apple 框架、macOS 自带的 SQLite 库，以及 MLX（mlx‑swift，MIT）及其依赖库 swift‑numerics（Apache 2.0）。MLX 在这台 Mac 上运行可选搜索模型和内置模型，这些模型只会在你提出要求时下载。完整列表见“致谢与许可”。";

